CHAPTER.VERS:
Now concerning spiritual [gifts], brothers, I would not have you

          {+}
         ignorant.

You

          {+}
         know that when you

          {+}
         were Gentiles [you

          {+}
         were] led away to those mute idols, however you

          {+}
         might be led.

Therefore I make known to you

          {+}
        , that no man speaking in the Spirit of God says, Accursed Jesus; and no man can say, Lord Jesus, but in the Holy Spirit.

And the eye can't say to the hand, I have no need of you: or again the head to the feet, I have no need of you

          {+}
        .

Now you

          {+}
         are the body of Christ, and severally members of it.

But desire earnestly the greater gifts. And moreover a most excellent way I show to you

          {+}
        .
